# Expand Growth Loop

L0/L1/L2 machinery lives in `path-sim`.

## Invariant (two composed loops)

∀ material judgment work: grow by **two composed loops at different timescales**, joined by a **distill** link:
- **inner** (inference-time · **fixed** substrate): **run → reflect** — one work item, searched under the current skills/rules/SOTs.
- **outer** (train-time · **substrate change**): **optimize → expand** — accrues across items; execution is a durable edit (mint/refine a skill, split/retire a rule, introduce a primitive).
- **distill** (inner → outer): amortize recurring inner-loop search residue into the substrate (a recurring consult pattern → a minted skill).

Path-sim L-layers are the **planning** operators (they search *what* to change); the outer loop's **execution** is the substrate edit itself. ¬ collapse every arc to L1-only patches when architecture suitability is live; ¬ conflate planning a restructure (inference-time L2) with executing it (train-time edit).

## LLM-edge mirror (why this exists)

Frontier reasoning does **not** natively widen: baseline self-verification/backtracking is <0.5% of solutions, elicited to ~13–26% only by scaffolds, and trained-in via RL for reasoning models. The loop shape comes from **scaffolding + training, not innate disposition** — which is exactly why the fleet needs explicit machinery (path-sim) rather than trusting an arc to widen on its own. (Bound: A-leg `opus-a-leg-answer.md`, bus 5267.)

| Loop | Step | Timescale · substrate | Path-sim layer (plan) · execution | Seat cue |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| inner | run | inference-time · fixed | execute the bound path | after A bind |
| inner | reflect | inference-time · fixed | critique/verify — carries an **external-vs-self signal axis** (see below) | R / code-review / friction |
| link | distill | inner → outer · amortize | search residue → minted skill / rule edit | recurring pattern → SOT |
| outer | optimize | train-time · refine | **L1** plans · execution = edit skill/rule | narrow fix / policy refine |
| outer | expand | train-time · change | **L0 ∧ L2** plan · execution = restructure (substrate/structure search) | when structure questioned ∨ detent ≥ `wide` |

**Reflect signal axis:** external-signal reflect (operator/cross-seat review, tests, quality gates — PRM-shaped) vs self-signal reflect (self-conformance checks, own friction logs — Reflexion-shaped). Self-graded-only loops inherit the dominant failure mode (self-critique without an external signal); flag them and prefer an external check.

**Expand (GROUNDED analogue — Opus A2, bus 5267):** outer-loop expand ↔ **substrate/structure search**, not curiosity/exploration. Primary analogue **NAS** (propose structure → run → held-out evaluate → refine the proposer); secondary **POET/QD** (minimal-criterion admission + novelty + transfer); **world-models** supply the model-edit vs learner-edit axis (ontology/rule edits vs skill/primitive edits). Evict: ICM/RND intrinsic-motivation exploration maps to the **inner** run→reflect loop over a fixed substrate — the expand↔exploration binding is **retired**. Standing disanalogy: fleet edits are discrete, legible, human/agent-ratified, gradient-free, multi-criteria (≠ scalar argmax); unlike POET the fleet does not author its own work items. Operational hook: mint only under a minimal criterion (neither redundant nor unexercised) and validate against work items it was not authored for. Falsifier: if real edits exercise none of these imports, demote to vocabulary. Detail: `cortex://notes/system/threads/expand-growth-loop-l0-fable/opus-expand-bind/answer.md`.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Every `judgment_required` → L1 patch only | L0 then L1∧L2 unless detent=`closed` |
| "Expand" = more files under same bad substrate | L2 ranks rename/split/retire/introduce primitive |
| Treat path-sim as transport-only Q→A→ship | Path-sim is the expand engine for the growth loop |
| Map all four steps onto inference-time layers (one loop) | Inner (run/reflect, fixed substrate) vs outer (optimize/expand, substrate edit); **distill** links them |
| Fold repeated search into nothing (no amortization) | Recurring inner-loop pattern → distill into a minted skill / rule edit |
| Copy L0/L1/L2 tables into this rule | `path-sim` owns L-layer tables |

